.TH "GINOT-REFRESH" "1" "" "Ginot HaIr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&ginot\-refresh \- Refresh public plans and render the static site.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\&PYTHONPATH=src python3 \-m ginot.refresh [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&Queries public planning services and writes snapshots, exports and site files. Run from the repository root with the project dependencies installed. This command does not file objections.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\&\-h, \-\-help
\&Show command help and exit without performing work.
.TP
\&\-\-council VALUE
\&Council boundary GeoJSON (WGS84). Default: data/council_ginot_hair.geojson.
.TP
\&\-\-out VALUE
\&Directory for generated exports and changes. Default: out.
.TP
\&\-\-site VALUE
\&Directory for the generated static site. Default: docs.
.TP
\&\-\-base\-url VALUE
\&Public site base URL. Default: https://reihlinstinct.github.io/ginot\-hair\-plans/.
.TP
\&\-\-snapshots VALUE
\&Directory for dated planning snapshots. Default: snapshots.
.TP
\&\-\-status VALUE
\&Local plan tracking status JSON. Default: data/plan_status.json.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\&0 on success or \-\-help. Invalid arguments return 2. Runtime failures return nonzero.
.SH NOTES
\&These manuals document existing Python entrypoints, not installed executable aliases. Internal CI, maintenance and developer scripts are not part of this manual package.
